  "caption": "Quinn's mornings came with a new soundtrack: creak. Knees, hands and heels all felt moody, so the plan was to rest everything forever. The aches stayed anyway.\n\nKay explained that through menopause, falling oestrogen can make joints, tendons and muscles achy, and muscle and bone can dip faster. It's common and often responds well to the right approach.\n\nWhat can help: strength training two to three times a week, loading sore tendons rather than resting them, a little impact and balance work for bones, and planning sessions around recovery. It's not too late to start in your 50s.\n\nSee your GP if new pain appears in many joints at once or several joints feel stiff in the mornings, as other conditions can look similar.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
